menu "Station: GNSS link"

    config GNSS_LINK_DEFAULT_BAUD
        int "Default receiver COM1 baud rate"
        range 9600 921600
        default 115200
        help
            Baud rate the link opens at when no rate is stored: a factory
            receiver's 115200. Boot listens at the stored rate first and scans
            the other rates only when nothing valid arrives. The receiver
            profile then moves COM1 to its own rate (460800 by default; above
            115200 the RX-full threshold is 64 B, see gnss_link_core.c).

    config GNSS_LINK_RX_BUF_SIZE
        int "UART driver RX buffer (bytes)"
        range 4096 65536
        default 32768
        help
            Software buffer behind the hardware FIFO (internal RAM). Must
            cover the longest time the RX task can be kept off the CPU at the
            highest baud rate in use: 32 KB is about 2.8 s at 115200 baud and
            0.7 s at 460800. PROVISIONAL, to be confirmed on hardware: the
            bench test (app update plus receiver package download while
            streaming) must end with zero buffer-full and FIFO-overflow
            events.

    config GNSS_LINK_RX_TASK_PRIO
        int "RX task priority"
        range 5 22
        default 18
        help
            Must stay above every caster and web task, so a network stall
            never starves the UART drain.

    config GNSS_LINK_RX_TASK_CORE
        int "RX task core (0/1)"
        range 0 1
        default 1
        help
            Wi-Fi runs on core 0; keeping the GNSS reader on core 1 isolates it
            from radio bursts. The UART interrupt is allocated on the same core.

    config GNSS_LINK_RX_TASK_STACK
        int "RX task stack (bytes)"
        range 3072 16384
        default 4096
        help
            Static stack in internal RAM. The sinks (hub publish, MSM
            inspection, reply matching) run on it. PROVISIONAL, to be
            confirmed on hardware from the task's stack high-water mark.

    config GNSS_LINK_BENCH_HOOKS
        bool "Bench hooks in the receiver link (bench builds only)"
        depends on BENCH_CONSOLE
        default y
        help
            Test hooks the bench console drives: an RX task stall (the
            reader sleeps without reading or feeding the task watchdog), a
            one-shot stall inside the next RAW-lease read, a recorder of
            frame and drain-pass times in a static PSRAM ring (read to
            published latency, drain behaviour after a stall, delay of each
            epoch against its MSM time), the loader prompt detector in
            report-only mode, and closing the UART driver so its reopen
            schedule installs it again. Nothing runs unless a bench command
            asks for it. The release job refuses a build with this on.

endmenu
